  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Pallorbund Tea Ltd vs Union Of India & Ors on 11 December, 2018 Author: Arindam Sinha Bench: Arindam Sinha Od-4 Order",
    "facts": "Petitioner has challenged letter dated 5th September, 2018 issued by the authority, by which it proposed to determine and recover in respect of petitioner's contribution under section 45A of Employees' State Insurance Act, 1948 aggregate of Rs.3,22,394/- for period of default June, 2013 to May, 2018 in respect of 9 covered employees.",
    "arguments": "Mr. Debapriya Gupta, learned advocate appears on behalf of petitioner and submits by drawing attention to licence dated 26th September, 2017 issued by Government of India, Food Safety & Pallorbund Tea Ltd vs Union Of India & Ors on 11 December, 2018 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/81712683/ 1 Standards Authority of India, petitioner is engaged in business of manufacturer of tea. He submits, registered office of petitioner is situate in Kolkata while its factory is in Assam. According to him, the Act does not apply to seasonal factories. Sub-section (19A) in section 2 covers petitioner as a factory exclusively engaged in manufacture of tea, as a seasonal factory. Extension of prevision of this Act by State cannot make it become applicable to its factory. He seeks interference. Mr. Subal Maitra, learned advocate appears on behalf of the authority and submits, petitioner's establishment in Kolkata has been inspected and nine employees found covered. He seeks adjournment to produce notification and its schedule to show that petitioner's office is an establishment covered by the extension.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Mr. Debapriya Gupta, learned advocate appears on behalf of petitioner and submits by drawing attention to licence dated 26th September, 2017 issued by Government of India, Food Safety & Pallorbund Tea Ltd vs Union Of India & Ors on 11 December, 2018 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/81712683/ 1 Standards Authority of India, petitioner is engaged in business of manufacturer of tea. He submits, registered office of petitioner is situate in Kolkata while its factory is in Assam. According to him, the Act does not apply to seasonal factories. Sub-section (19A) in section 2 covers petitioner as a factory exclusively engaged in manufacture of tea, as a seasonal factory. Extension of prevision of this Act by State cannot make it become applicable to its factory. He seeks interference. Mr. Subal Maitra, learned advocate appears on behalf of the authority and submits, petitioner's establishment in Kolkata has been inspected and nine employees found covered. He seeks adjournment to produce notification and its schedule to show that petitioner's office is an establishment covered by the extension.",
